---
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
import { toneVar } from '../seqflow/tones';
import { pageLang } from '../../../utils/lang';

const ru = pageLang(Astro.url) === 'ru';

// Part of the built-in exception hierarchy of Python 3.14 (Lib/test/exception_hierarchy.txt, the documentation's
// "Exception hierarchy"). Each class is listed with its direct base; checked against issubclass on CPython 3.14.7.
const base: Record<string, string> = {
  SystemExit: 'BaseException', KeyboardInterrupt: 'BaseException', GeneratorExit: 'BaseException', BaseExceptionGroup: 'BaseException', Exception: 'BaseException',
  ArithmeticError: 'Exception', ZeroDivisionError: 'ArithmeticError',
  LookupError: 'Exception', IndexError: 'LookupError', KeyError: 'LookupError',
  OSError: 'Exception', FileNotFoundError: 'OSError', PermissionError: 'OSError',
  ValueError: 'Exception', UnicodeError: 'ValueError', UnicodeDecodeError: 'UnicodeError',
  TypeError: 'Exception', AttributeError: 'Exception', StopIteration: 'Exception', RuntimeError: 'Exception', ExceptionGroup: 'Exception',
};
const top = ['SystemExit', 'KeyboardInterrupt', 'GeneratorExit', 'BaseExceptionGroup', 'Exception'];
const cats: [string, string[]][] = [
  ['ArithmeticError', ['ZeroDivisionError']],
  ['LookupError', ['IndexError', 'KeyError']],
  ['OSError', ['FileNotFoundError', 'PermissionError']],
  ['ValueError', ['UnicodeError', 'UnicodeDecodeError']],
];
const loose = ['TypeError', 'AttributeError', 'StopIteration', 'RuntimeError', 'ExceptionGroup'];
for (const [c, kids] of cats) { if (base[c] !== 'Exception') throw new Error(c); kids.forEach((k, i) => { if (base[k] !== (i === 0 ? c : c === 'ValueError' ? 'UnicodeError' : c)) throw new Error(`${k} under ${c}`); }); }
for (const k of [...top, ...loose]) if (!base[k]) throw new Error(k);

const t = ru
  ? { nb: 'в обычном коде их не ловят', ex: 'except Exception ловит всё ниже' }
  : { nb: 'do not catch these in ordinary code', ex: 'except Exception catches all below' };

// Narrow layout: an indented tree. Rows in depth-first order.
const rows: [number, string][] = [[0, 'BaseException'], ...top.slice(0, 4).map((n) => [1, n] as [number, string]), [1, 'Exception']];
for (const [c, kids] of cats) { rows.push([2, c]); kids.forEach((k, i) => rows.push([c === 'ValueError' && i === 1 ? 4 : 3, k])); }
for (const k of loose) rows.push([2, k]);
const toneOf = (name: string) => (name === 'BaseException' ? toneVar.n : top.slice(0, 4).includes(name) ? toneVar.y : name === 'Exception' ? toneVar.h : cats.some(([c]) => c === name) ? toneVar.g : toneVar.n);

// Wide layout: boxes. Row 1 holds the five direct subclasses of BaseException; under Exception, five columns.
const W = 760, cw = 6.5, bh = 26;
const boxW = (s: string) => s.length * cw + 18;
const row1Y = 74, busY = 140, catY = 158, gap = 30;
const xs1: number[] = [];
{
  const total = top.reduce((a, s) => a + boxW(s), 0) + 4 * 18;
  let x = (W - total) / 2;
  for (const s of top) { xs1.push(x); x += boxW(s) + 18; }
  if (xs1[0] < 4 || x - 18 > W - 4) throw new Error('row 1 does not fit');
}
const colX = [12, 162, 312, 462, 612];
const colW = 136;
for (const [c, kids] of cats) for (const s of [c, ...kids]) if (boxW(s) > colW) throw new Error(`${s} too wide`);
for (const s of loose) if (boxW(s) > colW) throw new Error(`${s} too wide`);
const H = catY + 5 * gap + 10;
const rowH = 22, NH = rows.length * rowH + 52;
const narrowRight = 356;
for (const [d, n] of rows) if (14 + d * 22 + n.length * 7.3 + 8 > narrowRight) throw new Error(`${n} overflows the narrow tree`);
const id = 'exc-hierarchy';
---

<Figure
  id={id}
  title={ru ? 'Иерархия встроенных исключений (часть)' : 'The built-in exception hierarchy (part)'}
  caption={ru
    ? 'Часть иерархии встроенных исключений Python 3.14. except C ловит исключения класса C и всех его потомков: except LookupError ловит и IndexError, и KeyError, а except OSError — FileNotFoundError и PermissionError. Красные классы наследуют прямо от BaseException, а не от Exception, поэтому except Exception их не перехватывает: Ctrl-C (KeyboardInterrupt) и sys.exit() (SystemExit) должны останавливать программу. ExceptionGroup наследует и от Exception, и от BaseExceptionGroup. Жёлтым отмечены классы-категории, которые удобно ловить целиком.'
    : 'Part of the built-in exception hierarchy of Python 3.14. except C catches exceptions of class C and of every class below it: except LookupError catches both IndexError and KeyError, and except OSError catches FileNotFoundError and PermissionError. The red classes derive from BaseException directly, not from Exception, so except Exception does not intercept them: Ctrl-C (KeyboardInterrupt) and sys.exit() (SystemExit) must be able to stop the program. ExceptionGroup derives from both Exception and BaseExceptionGroup. Amber marks the category classes that are convenient to catch as a whole.'}
>
  <svg class="fig-wide" viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-labelledby={`${id}-w-t ${id}-w-d`}>
    <title id={`${id}-w-t`}>{ru ? 'Дерево классов исключений' : 'A tree of exception classes'}</title>
    <desc id={`${id}-w-d`}>{ru
      ? 'BaseException наверху. Под ним SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt, GeneratorExit, BaseExceptionGroup и Exception. Под Exception пять столбцов: ArithmeticError с ZeroDivisionError; LookupError с IndexError и KeyError; OSError с FileNotFoundError и PermissionError; ValueError с UnicodeError и UnicodeDecodeError; и TypeError, AttributeError, StopIteration, RuntimeError, ExceptionGroup.'
      : 'BaseException at the top. Below it SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt, GeneratorExit, BaseExceptionGroup and Exception. Below Exception, five columns: ArithmeticError with ZeroDivisionError; LookupError with IndexError and KeyError; OSError with FileNotFoundError and PermissionError; ValueError with UnicodeError and UnicodeDecodeError; and TypeError, AttributeError, StopIteration, RuntimeError, ExceptionGroup.'}</desc>
    {(() => {
      const rx = W / 2 - boxW('BaseException') / 2;
      const exX = xs1[4] + boxW('Exception') / 2;
      const box = (x: number, y: number, s: string, w = boxW(s)) => (
        <g>
          <rect x={x} y={y} width={w} height={bh} rx="5" style={`fill: ${toneOf(s)}; fill-opacity: 0.13; stroke: ${toneOf(s)}; stroke-width: 1.2`} />
          <text class="f-small" x={x + w / 2} y={y + bh / 2 + 4.5} text-anchor="middle">{s}</text>
        </g>
      );
      return (
        <g>
          {box(rx, 16, 'BaseException')}
          <path class="f-thin" d={`M ${W / 2} ${16 + bh} V ${row1Y - 14} M ${xs1[0] + boxW(top[0]) / 2} ${row1Y - 14} H ${exX}`} />
          {top.map((s, i) => (
            <g>
              <path class="f-thin" d={`M ${xs1[i] + boxW(s) / 2} ${row1Y - 14} V ${row1Y}`} />
              {box(xs1[i], row1Y, s)}
            </g>
          ))}
          <text class="f-small f-t-red" x={xs1[0]} y={row1Y + bh + 18}>{t.nb}</text>
          <text class="f-small f-t-blue" x={xs1[4] + boxW('Exception')} y={row1Y + bh + 18} text-anchor="end">{t.ex}</text>
          <path class="f-thin" d={`M ${exX} ${row1Y + bh} V ${row1Y + bh + 4} M ${exX} ${row1Y + bh + 24} V ${busY} M ${colX[0] + colW / 2} ${busY} H ${colX[4] + colW / 2}`} />
          {cats.map(([c, kids], j) => (
            <g>
              <path class="f-thin" d={`M ${colX[j] + colW / 2} ${busY} V ${catY}`} />
              {box(colX[j], catY, c, colW)}
              {kids.map((k, i) => {
                const depth = c === 'ValueError' ? i + 1 : 1;
                const x = colX[j] + 10 * depth, y = catY + (i + 1) * gap;
                return (
                  <g>
                    <path class="f-thin" d={`M ${x - 4} ${y - gap + bh} V ${y + bh / 2} H ${x + 2}`} />
                    {box(x + 2, y, k, colW - 10 * depth - 2)}
                  </g>
                );
              })}
            </g>
          ))}
          <path class="f-thin" d={`M ${colX[4] + colW / 2} ${busY} V ${catY}`} />
          {loose.map((s, i) => box(colX[4], catY + i * gap, s, colW))}
        </g>
      );
    })()}
  </svg>
  <svg class="fig-narrow seq-narrow" viewBox={`0 0 360 ${NH}`} role="img" aria-labelledby={`${id}-n-t ${id}-n-d`}>
    <title id={`${id}-n-t`}>{ru ? 'Дерево классов исключений' : 'A tree of exception classes'}</title>
    <desc id={`${id}-n-d`}>{ru
      ? 'Дерево с отступами: BaseException; под ним SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt, GeneratorExit, BaseExceptionGroup и Exception; под Exception категории ArithmeticError, LookupError, OSError и ValueError со своими потомками и классы TypeError, AttributeError, StopIteration, RuntimeError, ExceptionGroup.'
      : 'An indented tree: BaseException; under it SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt, GeneratorExit, BaseExceptionGroup and Exception; under Exception the categories ArithmeticError, LookupError, OSError and ValueError with their subclasses, and the classes TypeError, AttributeError, StopIteration, RuntimeError, ExceptionGroup.'}</desc>
    {rows.map(([d, n], i) => {
      const y = 24 + i * rowH;
      const parentRow = rows.slice(0, i).map(([pd], pi) => [pd, pi] as [number, number]).filter(([pd]) => pd === d - 1).pop();
      return (
        <g>
          {d !== 0 && parentRow && <path class="f-thin f-muted" d={`M ${14 + (d - 1) * 22 + 6} ${24 + parentRow[1] * rowH + 6} V ${y - 4} H ${14 + d * 22 - 4}`} />}
          <rect x={14 + d * 22} y={y - 14} width={n.length * 7.3 + 8} height={19} rx="4" style={`fill: ${toneOf(n)}; fill-opacity: 0.13; stroke: none`} />
          <text class="f-small" x={14 + d * 22 + 4} y={y}>{n}</text>
        </g>
      );
    })}
    <text class="f-small f-t-red" x="14" y={NH - 26}>{t.nb}</text>
  </svg>
</Figure>
